  "description": "DAVZUX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H96 N8 O28 Tb6 2+,2(Cl1 1-),4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.558-3.964 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.71-112.65°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb6(L1)4(OH)4(MeOH)4]·2Cl·4MeOH (C84H112N8O32Cl2Tb6). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
